      "writtenOn": "2025-05-15T21:06:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To make this easier to follow, the node name should match the `enum-name` property.  The `enum-name` is what is used by the AP power sequence driver.\n\nOption 1:\n```\n\tpwr-en-pp3300-a {\n```\n\nAlternately, if you want to capture the net name, you could use the net name as the node name, but create a node label matching the enum.\n\nOption 2:\n```\n\tpwr_en_pp3300_a: ec-pg3 {\n\n```\n\nThe variant (microchip/nuvoton/ite) overlay can reference power signal using the node label \n\n```\n\u0026pwr_en_pp330_a {\n\tgpios \u003d \u003cMCHP_GPIO_DECODE_226 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH\u003e;\n};\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "1464bab5c73ffbf0b0b9a2df5d9a664bce4adc69",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
